    "field": "Climate dynamics",
    "problem": "The cause of strong multidecadal sea surface temperature variability in the Western Tropical Pacific is poorly understood, particularly because the well-known Interdecadal Pacific Oscillation does not explain this phenomenon.",
    "method": "This study uses statistical analysis and a suite of Atlantic Pacemaker experiments with a coupled atmosphere-slab ocean model to demonstrate that western tropical Pacific multidecadal variability is remotely forced by the Atlantic multidecadal oscillation through an atmospheric teleconnection and local positive feedback.",
    "task": "This paper's task is to explain the cause of western tropical Pacific multidecadal sea surface temperature variability, demonstrating it is remotely forced by the Atlantic Multidecadal Oscillation through an atmospheric teleconnection using observational analysis and pacemaker experiments.",
